From: win4wine contributors
Subject: [PATCH] uxtheme/user32: render themed external-shell non-client frames

Keep Wine's existing geometry and non-client hit testing, rendering the
user's Window theme for opted-in external-shell caption and outer frame.
The export accepts a caller DC for WM_PRINT or uses a window DC for normal
painting. Classic and ordinary Wine sessions retain existing behavior.
Virtual native-client maximization is indicated by Win4WineMaximized.
Use actual theme caption/button image sizes and scaled two-pixel gaps,
sharing the exact rectangles with NC hit testing. Route tracked caption
button press drawing through the existing user-mode theme hook and update
NC hover state on mouse transitions. Keep classic virtual
maximization restore glyphs consistent with their action.
Correct GetThemeSysColor's system-index to msstyles-property translation;
COLOR_CAPTIONTEXT is 9 while the stored TMT_CAPTIONTEXT metric is 1610.
Public API reference:
https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/uxtheme/nf-uxtheme-getthemesyscolor

--- a/dlls/user32/defwnd.c
